{"body":"## Business Context & Purpose\n\nToday `rad-artifact serve` takes exactly one positional `<PATH>` (see [src/bin/rad-artifact.rs:858-961](src/bin/rad-artifact.rs#L858-L961) and the `command::Serve` definition at [src/bin/rad-artifact.rs:1686-1689](src/bin/rad-artifact.rs#L1686-L1689)). To seed a release that contains several artifacts (binary + signature + tarball, or a multi-target build matrix), a maintainer has to open one terminal per artifact, each running its own iroh endpoint, each registering its own `iroh://` location. That's friction for the most common \"I cut a release, please host all of it\" workflow.\n\nA single iroh `Server` already holds an `FsStore` that can host any number of blobs/collections (see [src/share/serve.rs](src/share/serve.rs)), so the underlying machinery is fine — the work is purely CLI ergonomics plus tracking N location registrations for cleanup.\n\n## Expected Behavior/Outcome\n\nOne `serve` invocation hosts many artifacts behind a single endpoint, registers one `iroh://` location per distinct release containing them, and retracts every registration cleanly on Ctrl+C. The user gets a single pre-flight summary instead of one prompt per file, and a single live status line while serving.\n\n## Proposed UX (priority order)\n\n1. **Variadic positional** — `rad-artifact serve <PATH>...`\n   Smallest diff, biggest payoff. Loops today's `compute_content_id` / `find_by_cid` logic over each arg. Ships first.\n\n2. **`--root <DIR>`** — `rad-artifact serve --root ./dist`\n   Walks the directory, hashes each entry, matches CIDs against known artifacts in releases, serves everything that matches. The killer feature for the \"I just downloaded the CI release bundle, host it\" case. Ships as a follow-up.\n\n3. **No-args interactive** — `rad-artifact serve` (TTY only)\n   Multi-select picker over releases/artifacts. Only useful when paired with `--root` since a picker without local bytes can't actually serve anything. Ships last (or not at all if `--root` covers the use case).\n\nAll three modes resolve to the same internal loop:\n\n1. Build a deduplicated `Vec<(path, cid, release_id)>` work list.\n2. Print a pre-flight table; prompt once to confirm (replacing the single `Confirm` at [src/bin/rad-artifact.rs:889](src/bin/rad-artifact.rs#L889)).\n3. Start one `Server`, run `add_blob` / `add_collection` per entry.\n4. Register one `iroh://` location per **distinct release** in the work list.\n5. On Ctrl+C, iterate the registration list and retract each.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `rad-artifact serve A B C` accepts multiple paths and serves them from one endpoint.\n- [ ] Duplicate CIDs in the input collapse to a single registration; per-CID release selection preserves today's \"most recent release wins\" behavior at [src/bin/rad-artifact.rs:876-882](src/bin/rad-artifact.rs#L876-L882).\n- [ ] A pre-flight table lists artifact name, short CID, and target release id; one combined confirmation prompt replaces N individual confirms.\n- [ ] Per-arg failure (path missing, CID not in any release, hash mismatch) is skipped with a warning rather than aborting; final output reports \"served N of M\".\n- [ ] Cleanup tracks every `(ReleaseId, Cid, Url)` registered and retracts each on shutdown; per-entry retract failures warn and continue rather than aborting cleanup of the rest.\n- [ ] Single-path invocations behave identically to today (no regression for the existing happy path).\n- [ ] `--no-input` continues to work: skips the confirm prompt, fails on any unresolved path.\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- **Key files**: [src/bin/rad-artifact.rs](src/bin/rad-artifact.rs) (`run_serve` at :858, `command::Serve` at :1686). No changes expected in [src/share/serve.rs](src/share/serve.rs) — the `Server` API already supports many `add_blob`/`add_collection` calls.\n- **Decision: skip-and-warn vs abort on per-arg failure.** Recommend skip-and-warn; matches the existing warning-on-cleanup style at [src/bin/rad-artifact.rs:944-956](src/bin/rad-artifact.rs#L944-L956), and is friendlier for long-running serve sessions where one stray path shouldn't tear everything down.\n- **Decision: register one location per distinct release.** A CID can appear in multiple releases (today the code picks the most-recent). Preserve that — fetchers union locations across releases anyway.\n- **Cleanup shape**: replace the single `(release_id, cid, url)` locals with `Vec<(ReleaseId, Cid, Url)>`; iterate on shutdown.\n- **Pre-flight table**: short CID + artifact name + release id, printed before the confirm prompt and before binding the endpoint, so users can abort cheaply.\n\n## Staging\n\n- **PR 1**: variadic-positional only. Loop + pre-flight table + dedup + multi-registration cleanup. Closes the 80% case.\n- **PR 2**: `--root <DIR>` directory walk and CID match. Independent of PR 1.\n- **PR 3 (optional)**: no-args interactive multi-select, gated on TTY, layered over PR 2.","type":"comment"}